#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/029_herbs_for_the_lakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Herbs for the Lakes"
msgstr "Örter till sjöarna"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/029_herbs_for_the_lakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Autumn comes, and the animals catch colds. Take my herbs to those who need them: two bundles to "
"the horse farm, two to the herders, two to Gudrun's inn."
msgstr ""
"Hösten kommer, och djuren blir förkylda. Ta mina örter till dem som behöver dem: två knippor till "
"hästgården, två till herdarna och två till Gudruns värdshus."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/029_herbs_for_the_lakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Herbs from Tova! Now the cow and the calf stay well all winter."
msgstr "Örter från Tova! Nu håller sig kon och kalven friska hela vintern."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/029_herbs_for_the_lakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "All delivered? You are real helpers now. Take these herbs for your own animals."
msgstr ""
"Allt levererat? Nu är {crew|du en riktig hjälpare|du en riktig hjälpare|ni riktiga hjälpare}. Ta "
"de här örterna till {crew|dina|dina|era} egna djur."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/029_herbs_for_the_lakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Herbs"
msgstr "Örter"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
