#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/029_herbs_for_the_lakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Healers dried herbs in bundles under the roof, to have them all winter."
msgstr "Läkekunniga torkade örter i knippor under taket, för att ha dem hela vintern."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Mill Turns"
msgstr "Kvarnen snurrar"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The harvest is in, and the mill wheel turns day and night! But the farmers are slow. Bring me six "
"crates of grain to grind."
msgstr ""
"Skörden är bärgad, och kvarnhjulet snurrar dag och natt! Men bönderna är långsamma. Ta hit sex "
"lådor säd att mala."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Six crates! Listen to the stones grind. Bjarne says hello, and here is your share."
msgstr "Sex lådor! Hör hur stenarna maler. Bjarne hälsar, och här är {crew|din|din|er} del."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Most vikings ground their grain by hand with two stones; a water mill was a wonder."
msgstr "De flesta vikingar malde säden för hand mellan två stenar; en vattenkvarn var ett under."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Henhouse Full"
msgstr "Fullt hönshus"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Eggs sell so well! Let us have six hens. Buy hens at the market in Kråkhamn or the farm of "
"Frosttorp, and bring them home."
msgstr ""
"Äggen säljer så bra! Låt oss skaffa sex hönor. Köp hönor på marknaden i Kråkhamn eller på gården i"
" Frosttorp, och ta hem dem."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Six hens! Cluck, cluck, scratch, scratch. Do not forget: they eat grain."
msgstr "Sex hönor! Kluck, kluck, krafs, krafs. Glöm inte: de äter säd."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking hens were small and laid fewer eggs than ours, but every farm had some."
msgstr "Vikingarnas hönor var små och värpte färre ägg än våra, men varje gård hade några."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey Cakes"
msgstr "Honungskakor"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We want to sell honey cakes on the market! But we have no oven. Bring honey and grain to your "
"grandmother; she bakes them overnight, and you bring us the cakes."
msgstr ""
"Vi vill sälja honungskakor på marknaden! Men vi har ingen ugn. Ta honung och säd till "
"{crew|din|din|er} farmor; hon bakar dem under natten, och sedan tar {crew|du|du|ni} kakorna till "
"oss."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey! Now the grain."
msgstr "Honung! Nu säden."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "I bake them tonight. Come for them in the morning!"
msgstr "Jag bakar dem i kväll. Kom och hämta dem i morgon bitti!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Still warm. Do not eat them all on the way!"
msgstr "Fortfarande varma. Ät inte upp allihop på vägen!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "They smell so good! Everybody comes to our stall. Here, half the silver is yours."
msgstr ""
"De doftar så gott! Alla kommer till vårt stånd. Här, hälften av silvret är {crew|ditt|ditt|ert}."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cakes"
msgstr "Kakor"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a basket of honey cakes|{count} baskets of honey cakes}"
msgstr "{count|en korg honungskakor|{count} korgar honungskakor}"

#. the thing '{count|a basket of honey cakes|{count} baskets of honey cakes}' for {thing@acc} in the
#. translations: the accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty
#. if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
