msgid "{count|a basket of honey cakes|{count} baskets of honey cakes}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking bread was flat and baked on hot stones; honey made it a treat."
msgstr "Vikingarnas bröd var platt och bakades på heta stenar; med honung blev det en godbit."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Chieftain's Feast"
msgstr "Hövdingens fest"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My daughter Thora turns twelve! A feast with the whole valley: bring me three crates of mead and "
"two of cheese, within three days."
msgstr ""
"Min dotter Tora fyller tolv! En fest för hela dalen: ta hit tre lådor mjöd och två lådor ost, inom"
" tre dagar."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The mead! The skalds will sing."
msgstr "Mjödet! Skalderna kommer att sjunga."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cheese, mead, songs and a fire! Come in, sit by me: it is the best birthday ever."
msgstr ""
"Ost, mjöd, sånger och en eld! Kom in, sitt bredvid mig: det är den bästa födelsedagen någonsin."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/033_the_chieftains_feast/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A chieftain's hall had a long fire in the middle, and benches along the walls."
msgstr "I en hövdings hall brann en lång eld i mitten, och längs väggarna stod bänkar."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Ferryman's Tale"
msgstr "Färjkarlens saga"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Old Halvard told a story here last night: a hidden cove, where the swans of the lakes are born. He"
" says: ask the potter, the miller and the old man of Svanetorp."
msgstr ""
"Gamle Halvard berättade en saga här i går kväll: om en dold vik där sjöarnas svanar föds. Han "
"säger: fråga krukmakaren, mjölnaren och gubben i Svanetorp."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The cove? My grandmother said: it lies where the reeds grow tallest. Ask Astrid."
msgstr "Viken? Min farmor sa: den ligger där vassen växer högst. Fråga Astrid."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Reeds? The tallest ones grow south, by Svanetorp. Go to Grim."
msgstr "Vass? Den högsta växer i söder, vid Svanetorp. Gå till Grim."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"So you found my secret. Behind my farm, in the reeds: the swan cove. Look, the cygnets! Grey and "
"fluffy. Tell no one!"
msgstr ""
"Så {crew|du|du|ni} hittade min hemlighet. Bakom min gård, i vassen: svanviken. Titta, ungarna! Grå"
" och fluffiga. Säg det inte till någon!"

#. a gift for a task: 'You get ...'
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "the secret of the swan cove"
msgstr "hemligheten om svanviken"

#. the thing 'the secret of the swan cove' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the
#. direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain
#. translation
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "the secret of the swan cove"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/034_the_ferrymans_tale/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Young swans are grey, not white; they are called cygnets."
msgstr "Unga svanar är grå, inte vita; de kallas svanungar."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Wool for the Winter Cloth"
msgstr "Ull till vintertyget"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Everybody wants warm cloth for the winter, and my looms are hungry. Bring me four crates of wool, "
"and I give you a bolt of red cloth."
msgstr ""
"Alla vill ha varmt tyg till vintern, och mina vävstolar är hungriga. Ta hit fyra lådor ull, så ger"
" jag {crew|dig|dig|er} en rulle rött tyg."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Clack, clack, goes the loom. Here: the reddest cloth I ever made, for you."
msgstr ""
"Klapp, klapp, säger vävstolen. Här: det rödaste tyg jag någonsin har vävt, åt {crew|dig|dig|er}."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/035_wool_for_the_winter_cloth/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The women of a viking farm wove all the cloth: sails, clothes and blankets."
msgstr "Kvinnorna på en vikingagård vävde allt tyg: segel, kläder och filtar."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flax in the Field"
msgstr "Lin på åkern"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Linen is softer than wool on the skin. Plant flax on your farm! When it blooms blue and is ripe, "
"bring me two crates."
msgstr ""
"Linne är mjukare än ull mot huden. Så lin på {crew|din|din|er} gård! När det blommar blått och är "
"moget, ta hit två lådor."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flax seed in the field. In a few days, it blooms blue."
msgstr "Linfrö i åkern. Om några dagar blommar det blått."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Your own flax! I will make you linen shirts, soft as a cloud."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Ditt|Ditt|Ert} eget lin! Jag syr linneskjortor åt {crew|dig|dig|er}, mjuka som ett moln."

#. a gift for a task: 'You get ...'
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "linen shirts"
msgstr "linneskjortor"

#. the thing 'linen shirts' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative (the direct object),
#. e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "linen shirts"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/036_flax_in_the_field/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Flax was soaked, beaten and combed for weeks before it could be spun into linen."
msgstr "Linet blöttes, bråkades och häcklades i veckor innan det kunde spinnas till linne."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Barley for the Brewer"
msgstr "Korn till bryggaren"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Orm of Hallvik wants the biggest barrel of ale for the autumn feast. I need grain, five crates! "
"Bring them, and you get two crates of my ale."
msgstr ""
"Orm i Hallvik vill ha den största öltunnan till höstfesten. Jag behöver säd, fem lådor! Ta hit "
"dem, så får {crew|du|du|ni} två lådor av mitt öl."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Into the water with it, let it sprout... In a week, the best ale of the lakes!"
msgstr "Ner i vattnet med det, låt det gro... Om en vecka: det bästa ölet på sjöarna!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/037_barley_for_the_brewer/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ale was brewed from barley and water, often with herbs instead of hops."
msgstr "Öl bryggdes på korn och vatten, ofta med örter i stället för humle."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Proper Hold"
msgstr "Ett riktigt lastrum"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You are real traders now: you need a real hold! Bring me eight planks from Frosttorp and two "
"crates of iron tools, and pay 20 silver. Then your hold takes two more crates."
msgstr ""
"Nu är {crew|du en riktig handlare|du en riktig handlare|ni riktiga handlare}: då behövs ett "
"riktigt lastrum! Ta hit åtta plankor från Frosttorp och två lådor järnverktyg, och betala 20 "
"silver. Då rymmer {crew|ditt|ditt|ert} lastrum två lådor till."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Planks of pine, split with wedges. Stack them well!"
msgstr "Tallplankor, kluvna med kilar. Stapla dem ordentligt!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Good iron! Now my wages."
msgstr "Bra järn! Nu min lön."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Saw, plane, rivets... Look at her! Longer, wider, and room for two more crates."
msgstr "Såg, hyvel, nitar... Titta på henne! Längre, bredare, och plats för två lådor till."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Plank"
msgstr "Planka"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a plank|{count} planks}"
msgstr "{count|en planka|{count} plankor}"

#. the thing '{count|a plank|{count} planks}' for {thing@acc} in the translations: the accusative
#. (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty if it is the same as the
#. plain translation
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
msgctxt "acc"
msgid "{count|a plank|{count} planks}"
msgstr ""

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/038_a_proper_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking boats were built of overlapping planks, held with iron rivets."
msgstr "Vikingabåtar byggdes av plankor som låg omlott, hopfästa med järnnitar."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Messenger's Cold"
msgstr "Budbärarens förkylning"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Atchoo! I have a cold, and I must tell the smith, the horse farm and the herders about the autumn "
"feast at Hallvik. Can you do it today? Atchoo!"
msgstr ""
"Atjo! Jag är förkyld, och jag måste berätta för smeden, hästgården och herdarna om höstfesten i "
"Hallvik. Kan {crew|du|du|ni} göra det i dag? Atjo!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The autumn feast? I will bring my best knives to show."
msgstr "Höstfesten? Jag tar med mina bästa knivar och visar dem."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "We will come with all the horses! Tell Inga to drink hot honey water."
msgstr "Vi kommer med alla hästarna! Säg åt Inga att dricka varmt honungsvatten."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A feast! I will bring my flute. Thank you!"
msgstr "En fest! Jag tar med min flöjt. Tack!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/039_the_messengers_cold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Messengers rowed, rode and ran: news could cross a land in a few days."
msgstr "Budbärare rodde, red och sprang: nyheter kunde färdas genom ett helt land på några dagar."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hay for Frosttorp"
msgstr "Hö till Frosttorp"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My hay meadow was flooded, and the cows are hungry! I need eight crates of hay. Your big boat can "
"do it in one trip."
msgstr ""
"Min äng blev översvämmad, och korna är hungriga! Jag behöver åtta lådor hö. {crew|Din|Din|Er} "
"stora båt klarar det på en tur."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Moo! Listen to them, they are happy. You saved my winter. Take this cheese."
msgstr ""
"Mu! Hör på dem, de är glada. {crew|Du räddade|Du räddade|Ni räddade} min vinter. Ta den här osten."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/040_hay_for_frosttorp/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hay is dried grass; without enough of it, a farm could not keep its animals over winter."
msgstr "Hö är torkat gräs; utan tillräckligt med hö kunde en gård inte föda sina djur över vintern."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sigvor's Cheese"
msgstr "Sigvors ost"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My goats gave so much milk this summer! I made four big wheels of cheese for Orm's autumn feast in"
" Hallvik, but my boat is full of goats. Will you carry them?"
msgstr ""
"Mina getter gav så mycket mjölk i somras! Jag gjorde fyra stora ostar till Orms höstfest i "
"Hallvik, men min båt är full av getter. Vill {crew|du|du|ni} frakta dem?"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sigvor's cheese! The guests will fight over it. Well, not fight: they will ask nicely."
msgstr "Sigvors ost! Gästerna kommer att slåss om den. Nja, inte slåss: de kommer att fråga snällt."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Roll them in gently. And no nibbling!"
msgstr "Rulla in dem försiktigt. Och inget smakande!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/041_sigvors_cheese/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cheese"
msgstr "Ost"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
