#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/090_gudruns_ring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Vikings sometimes gave silver to the lakes on purpose, as gifts to the gods."
msgstr "Vikingarna gav ibland silver till sjöarna med flit, som gåvor till gudarna."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Edge of the Forest"
msgstr "Skogskanten"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Kol and Ingrid want sheep for their new home. Bring them two sheep, and I give you the strip of "
"land by the forest, next to your farm. A fair trade!"
msgstr ""
"Kol och Ingrid vill ha får till sitt nya hem. Ta två får till dem, så ger jag {crew|dig|dig|er} "
"marken vid skogen, bredvid {crew|din|din|er} gård. Ett rättvist byte!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Two sheep for the young ones! Ingrid already knits. The forest edge is yours: good wood and two "
"fields."
msgstr ""
"Två får till de unga! Ingrid stickar redan. Skogskanten är {crew|din|din|er}: bra virke och två "
"åkrar."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/091_the_edge_of_the_forest/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Land was traded for animals, silver or work: there were no banks."
msgstr "Mark byttes mot djur, silver eller arbete: det fanns inga banker."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Longhouse Grows"
msgstr "Långhuset växer"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"With so many animals and friends, our house is too small! Bring twelve logs from Frosttorp, two "
"crates of tools and two pots of tar, and we make it longer."
msgstr ""
"Med så många djur och vänner är vårt hus för litet! Ta hit tolv stockar från Frosttorp, två lådor "
"verktyg och två krukor tjära, så bygger vi ut det."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Twelve logs! Fill that big hold of yours."
msgstr "Tolv stockar! Fyll {crew|ditt|ditt|ert} stora lastrum."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Axes and nails. Now the tar for the roof."
msgstr "Yxor och spikar. Nu tjäran till taket."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hammering all night with the neighbours... Our longhouse is twice as long! Room for a feast."
msgstr "Hamrande hela natten med grannarna... Vårt långhus är dubbelt så långt! Plats för en fest."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/092_the_longhouse_grows/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A longhouse could be made longer by adding a piece at the end, like a train."
msgstr "Ett långhus kunde göras längre genom att man byggde till en bit i änden, som ett tåg."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Green Valley"
msgstr "Den gröna dalen"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You helped my valley all year. The green valley behind your farm has no owner: bring me two crates"
" of cloth and two of honey for the gods' feast, and it is yours."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Du har|Du har|Ni har} hjälpt min dal hela året. Den gröna dalen bakom {crew|din|din|er} gård"
" har ingen ägare: ta hit två lådor tyg och två lådor honung till gudarnas fest, så blir den "
"{crew|din|din|er}."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cloth for the hall. Now the honey."
msgstr "Tyg till hallen. Nu honungen."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Father says it at the Thing, in front of everybody: the green valley belongs to Ylva and Sigrid!"
msgstr "Far säger det på tinget, inför alla: den gröna dalen tillhör Ylva och Sigrid!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/093_the_green_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "At the Thing, the meeting of the free people, land and laws were decided."
msgstr "På tinget, de fria människornas möte, bestämdes det om mark och lagar."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bees for the Valley"
msgstr "Bin till dalen"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The valley is full of clover and heather. Bees would love it! Have three beehives on the farm, and"
" we will have honey all year."
msgstr ""
"Dalen är full av klöver och ljung. Bina skulle älska den! Ha tre bikupor på gården, så får vi "
"honung hela året."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hum, hum, hum! Three hives in the valley. Honey for us, and for mead."
msgstr "Surr, surr, surr! Tre kupor i dalen. Honung åt oss, och till mjöd."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/094_bees_for_the_valley/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Heather honey is dark and strong; clover honey is light and mild."
msgstr "Ljunghonung är mörk och stark; klöverhonung är ljus och mild."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Apples for the Market"
msgstr "Äpplen till marknaden"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Thanks to the bees, my trees are full of apples! Twelve baskets for the market in Kråkhamn. Only "
"your boat can take them all at once."
msgstr ""
"Tack vare bina är mina träd fulla av äpplen! Tolv korgar till marknaden i Kråkhamn. Bara "
"{crew|din|din|er} båt kan ta dem alla på en gång."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Twelve baskets of apples! The whole market smells of autumn."
msgstr "Tolv korgar äpplen! Hela marknaden doftar höst."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/095_apples_for_the_market/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Red and green and yellow. Take one for the trip!"
msgstr "Röda och gröna och gula. Ta ett till resan!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
